      "value": "@{5b07d70c0cac326467244125|full_name}: I'm sorry I misunderstood your comment. It just seems that the structure of it makes it seem very sarcastic. You point out that you are concerned about breaking ToS, then go on to point out that everyone seems to do it, and no one is punished. That makes your first line seem sarcastic. Then you say \"+1 vote\" to the suggestion to remove the warning from the loading screen. I didn't mean anything bad by my comment, I was just trying to validate WHY the rule shouldn't be removed from the loading screen, even if people feel that it shouldn't be a rule in the first place (which isn't really an argument for here or now, anyway).",
